  m_Name: Spinocerebellar Ataxia Type 15 (SCA15)
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MedicalCase
  caseImage1: {fileID: -3289756831445821579, guid: 919115a684fc486458f4f4c915c965e6, type: 3}
  caseImage2: {fileID: 0}
  title: Spinocerebellar Ataxia Type 15 (SCA15)
  type: Uncommon
  category: Genetic Disorder / Neurological
  description: A rare genetic, hereditary ataxia that affects the cerebellum, leading
    to progressive neurological symptoms.
  symptoms: Difficulty walking with a wide-based, unsteady, ataxic gait.   Dysarthria
    (slow, slurred speech).   Intention tremors and dysmetria in upper limbs.   Mild
    spasticity, hyperreflexia, and saccadic eye movements.
  pathology: Associated with a pathogenic variant in the ITPR1 gene. It follows an
    autosomal dominant inheritance pattern and shows bilateral cerebellar atrophy
    on brain MRI.
  treatment: 'No cure is currently available.   Managed with physical therapy and
    occupational therapy to maintain function.   Formal genetic testing and genetic
    counseling for family members.  '
  keyFeatures: Recognized by progressive cerebellar ataxia, an autosomal dominant
    family history, and bilateral cerebellar atrophy.
  requiredStageLevel: 1
